    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Detailed History Butte was originally settled by homesteaders in the early 20th century, drawn by the fertile soil and proximity to the Matanuska River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://myalaskan.com/butte-alaska/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Butte hosts Alaska Raceway Park, a 1/3 mile asphalt oval that has operated for over 50 years and is NASCAR‑certified.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butte%2C_Alaska"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On Bodenburg Butte’s southern flank sits Williams Reindeer Farm, which has been operating since 1987.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
